    "result_text": "The full suite passes (AcceptanceTest is the only test class; the other files are a base class and a helper). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from the owner's city, following the project's existing read-time derivation pattern (the same approach used for `membershipTier`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` property (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `locality(Owner)` default method implementing the fixed table: `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other (or null) city.\n\n`locality` is derived at read time from the stored city \u2014 no entity/schema persistence change needed, consistent with the existing `displayName`/`initials`/`membershipTier` derivations.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. Both acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` expecting `NSW` for Sydney, and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` expecting `UNKNOWN`) pass.",
